 IN THE MATTER THE APPLICATION OF EL
 PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR REVISION
 OF   ITS  RETAIL   ELECTRIC    RATES
 PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE NO. 317
                                                                  Case No. 25-00082-UT
 EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY,

                 Applicant.

          JOINT MOTION OF EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY AND
    NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION ADVISORY STAFF TO
         MODIFY PROCEDURAL ORDER, VACATE DEADLINES AND
       ESTABLISH PROCEDURES FOR CONSIDERING A STIPULATION

       El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”) and New Mexico Public Regulation Commission

(“NMPRC” or “Commission”) Advisory Staff (“Staff”) (“Joint Movants”), pursuant to

Commission Rules 1.2.2.12(A) and 1.2.2.24(B) of the New Mexico Administrative Code

(“NMAC”) hereby file this Opposed Joint Motion to Modify the Procedural Schedule to vacate

the October 23, 2026 deadline to file Staff and intervenor direct testimony, vacate the November

30, 2026 deadline to file rebuttal testimony, and to establish additional procedures for considering

a stipulation. Due to current procedural schedule deadlines, Joint Movants seek a decision on this

request prior to the October 23, 2026 deadline for filing of Staff and intervenor direct testimony.

As grounds for this request, Joint Movants state the following:

       1.        On August 27, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued an Order Establishing Revised

Procedural Schedule (“Order”) establishing the following procedural deadlines relevant to this

Joint Motion:

            a. October 23, 2026: deadline for Staff and Intervenors to file direct testimony;

            b.   November 20, 2026: deadline to file rebuttal testimony;

            c. December 3, 2026: deadline to file a stipulation; and
               d. December 9 - 22, 2026: public hearing.

        2.       Joint Movants have entered into an agreement in principle in this matter which EPE

circulated to all parties on October 18, 2022. Joint Movants are engaged in further discussions

regarding whether additional parties are interested in joining a stipulation, and under what

conditions.

        3.       Joint Movants desire to focus limited resources on continuing settlement

negotiations without having to concurrently prepare direct and rebuttal testimony on EPE’s

Amended Application. Vacating the current procedural deadlines is more efficient because parts

of the Amended Application will be changed by the forthcoming stipulation.

        4.       Joint Movants are committed to pursuing their stipulation even if it is contested.

        5.       Rule 1.2.2.24(B) authorizes the Commission or presiding officer “to modify

procedural orders on their own motion or on motion of staff or a party when necessary.”

Additionally, the Order provides that “[a]dditional procedures will be set by separate order if a

stipulation is filed.”

        6.       Joint Movants, accordingly, move the Hearing Examiner to modify the Procedural

Order pursuant to Rule 1.2.2.24(B) to vacate the deadlines to file direct and rebuttal testimony and

establish additional procedures and corresponding deadlines for a stipulation.

        7.       Joint Movants request the following schedule for evaluating a stipulation. This

proposed schedule would keep the December 9 through 22, 2026 dates for a public hearing on a

stipulation:

 DEADLINE                                             ACTION
 Before October 30                                    Status Conference
 November 15                                          Deadline for Filing     a   Stipulation   and
                                                      Testimony in Support


Joint Motion to Amend Procedural Schedule
Docket No. 25-00082-UT
                                                  2
     November 20                                 Deadline to File Statements Opposing the
                                                Stipulation and Testimony in opposition to the
                                                Stipulation
    November 30                                 Deadline to File Stipulation Rebuttal
                                                Testimony
          Joint Movants have circulated this motion to parties and the positions provided are as

follows: the Coalition for Clean Affordable Energy1; City of Las Cruces, Doña Ana County2, New

Mexico Department of Justice, Dwight Eggers, and Stephen Fischmann oppose the request;

Walmart Inc takes no position; and Federal Executive Agencies (US DOD-FEA), Philip B.

Simpson, New Mexico State University, and Western Resource Advocates did not provide a

response in the time provided.

          WHEREFORE, based on the foregoing, and prior to the October 23, 2026 deadline for

Staff and intervenor direct testimony, Joint Movants respectfully request an order modifying the

Procedural Order to vacate the October 23, 2026 and November 30, 2026 deadlines to file Staff

and intervenor direct testimony and rebuttal testimonies and adopt the following proposed

schedule for additional procedures for a stipulation:

    Before October 30                                         Status Conference
    November 15                                               Deadline for Filing a Stipulation and
                                                              Testimony in Support
    November 20                                               Deadline to File Statements Opposing the
                                                              Stipulation and Testimony in opposition to the
                                                              Stipulation
    November 30                                               Deadline to File Stipulation Rebuttal
                                                              Testimony



1
  The Coalition for Clean Affordable Energy does not oppose settlement negotiations but requests that the direct
testimony deadline not be vacated
2
  “The County opposes the relief requested and does not believe it is realistic or wise to have a dispute over the
schedule 3 days before the critical testimony deadline. Further the proposed deadlines in the motion are unworkable
and will greatly prejudice intervenors if granted, causing parties to simultaneously negotiate a stipulation and revise
and modify testimony, during the holidays, to oppose a stipulation and prepare for hearing if consensus can’t be
reached.”


Joint Motion to Amend Procedural Schedule
Docket No. 25-00082-UT
